checkct	-	the `checkct` job in nightly.yml is workflow_dispatch-only + continue-on-error (WIP) and invokes cargo-checkct directly, NOT `make checkct` — so no workflow carries this target (runs_in dropped 2026-08-20, #664). The opam-released binsec can't build the ARM decoder + checkct plugin together (diagnosed 2026-06-29); needs a from-source binsec in a clean CI switch. Validated gate is LOCAL `make checkct`. Tracked in the nightly.yml comment + tools/sca/DONJON-RUST-TOOLING.md.
verify-extraction-regen	-	F1 (2026-07-16): the REAL regen check — re-runs charon->aeneas + diff for every extract-* target. Needs the §33 toolchain in ~/.local/share/pqsigner-lean (charon nightly-2026.06.08 + aeneas nightly-2026.06.10), which cannot run on a stock CI runner, so it stays LOCAL. The per-PR CI protection is the toolchain-free verify-extraction-freshness sha256 tripwire (above).
verify-lean4checker	-	Independent kernel/environment replay (~40-60 min per sweep; manual pre-release gate, last recorded run 2026-07-15 over 58 modules — the tree now has 59, exact-HEAD replay pending). Enrolled 2026-07-19 (FV deep review F5): previously unwired everywhere and escaped the completeness scan because no workflow invokes it. SCOPE: this is a replay, NOT an axiom-closure recomputation — its Replay re-adds referenced .axiomInfo as legal axioms, so the #8840 omission shape survives it (see scripts/run_lean4checker.sh header). The permitted-axioms allowlist backstop (e.g. nanoda_lib) is tracked as a follow-up.
verify-extracted-heavy	-	FormatDecimalSpec kernel type-checking needs about 42 GB RSS (measured 2026-07-07; carved out of the default target the same day). It is deliberately absent from the 16 GB hosted workflow: even a continue-on-error attempt can terminate the runner and suppress later mandatory evidence. Authoritative validation runs locally or on a >=48 GB runner. The mandatory extracted suite remains blocking.
verify-bytecode	-	the Halmos+z3 symbolic discharge of A3.2/A3.3/A3.4 needs the patched halmos toolchain + is slow (kept local/manual per ci.yml:20-23). Per-PR protection against wallet-bytecode drift is the codehash-freeze test/PinnedCodehashes.t.sol in the `contracts` job (forces a conscious re-pin); nothing auto-re-runs Halmos after a re-pin. Kontrol/KEVM is the independent transcription-free cross-check, also local. Corrected 2026-07-02: was advertised as 'the fast CI gate' but runs in NO workflow (HALMOS-FAST-CI-GATE-FALSE). The incorrect runs_in entry is removed under #664; no workflow invokes this make target.
verify-easycrypt	-	F5 (2026-07-16) enrolls the EasyCrypt +C port gate — previously the ONLY formal-verification surface absent from this manifest, so its skips/admits/axioms/dependency state were invisible to the G1-G5 controls. Needs the pinned opam ec-r2026 switch (EasyCrypt r2026.02 + Alt-Ergo 2.6.0) + the MM45 reference proofs, so it stays local-only. Split into three targets: verify-easycrypt (PARTIAL: stdlib +C chain, MM45-chain skipped loudly), verify-easycrypt-full (FULL: 21/21 zero skips, fails if MM45 refs absent), verify-easycrypt-pins (toolchain-free ledger: admit/axiom COUNT + SEMANTIC name->statement pin + a wired-in negative control that a dmkey_ll:false weakening MUST fire). The toolchain-free pin (verify-easycrypt-pins) is CI-wired per-PR in lean-fv.yml since 2026-08-20 (#664); the full compile cannot be (no MM45 docker on runners).
verify-three-claims	-	a LOCAL end-to-end convenience bundle (kernel + audit + lints + forge + Halmos/Certora advisory), NOT a single CI job. Its dead nested workflow (contracts/.github/... — GitHub never ran it) was removed 2026-07-02 (F1). Its constituent gates ARE per-PR: verify-build/audit/fv-lints/ledger-consistency/storage-mutators (lean-fv.yml), verify-transcription (a31-transcription.yml), forge test + codehash-freeze (ci.yml); the Halmos/Kontrol legs are verify-bytecode (also local_documented).
verify-mmio-addresses	-	diffs the hand-transcribed MMIO bases against ST's own CMSIS stm32u585xx.h, which lives in an STM32CubeU5 vendor checkout that is never present on CI runners. scripts/check_mmio_addresses.py SKIP-exits 0 when the header is absent, so the ci.yml step was a permanent green no-op asserting nothing (F51) — removed from ci.yml 2026-07-19. The gate stays a REAL check on every dev box with the vendor SDK (point STM32U5_CMSIS_HEADER= at the header), which is every machine that builds the hw targets.
kani-heavy	-	The three 100-byte-symbolic multiSend harnesses (per_record_page_bound 12.71 GiB/6m03s, no_hidden_value 13.05 GiB/7m55s, cow_presign_precedence 11.50 GiB/3m56s; all VERIFY SUCCESSFULLY, measured locally 2026-07-31) exceed what a hosted runner can absorb. Instrumented CI evidence 2026-07-31: the runner has 15,989 MB RAM with 14,497 MB available and 145 GB disk with 86 GB free, so DISK IS NOT THE CAUSE - it is memory. The kill lands between 'Runtime Postprocess Equation' and 'Solving with ...', i.e. inside CBMC's formula construction and BEFORE any SAT solver is invoked; a kissat experiment was therefore reverted, since the solver never runs. (That experiment's local peak-RSS numbers were also unsound: an external solver runs out-of-process and /usr/bin/time -v reports a per-process maximum, not an aggregate.) Excluded because an OOM kills the runner and suppresses every later mandatory gate in the same job - same reasoning as verify-extracted-heavy (53c19f21); continue-on-error cannot save a dead runner. The 100-byte bound is deliberately NOT reduced: shrinking a proof's bound to earn a green check is coverage loss disguised as a pass. Larger hosted runners are unavailable (Team/Enterprise-only; this org is free-plan; hosted-runners API 404s). Run via `make kani-heavy`; the other 170 harnesses stay blocking in nightly. runs_in=nightly.yml dropped 2026-08-20 (#664) — no workflow invokes the target.
verify-easycrypt-full	-	FULL EasyCrypt verification (21/21 .ec compiled as targets, ZERO skips) needs the pinned opam ec-r2026 switch (EasyCrypt r2026.02 + Alt-Ergo 2.6.0) AND the MM45 reference proofs, and FAILS by design when either is absent — so it cannot run on a stock runner (F5 split, 2026-07-16). The toolchain-free ledger leg (verify-easycrypt-pins) is per-PR in lean-fv.yml. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-easycrypt-docker	-	the C10-concrete capstone reproduces MM45's confirmed toolchain (EC r2026.02 + Z3 4.13.4 + Alt-Ergo 2.6.0) in docker and needs a local MM45 checkout (C10_PORT_DIR with its FV-SPHINCSPLUS-EC submodule — third-party, not vendored); absent either it prints the committed 2026-07-17 gate receipt and SKIP-exits 0, which as a CI step would be a permanent green no-op. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-tla	-	needs a local tla2tools.jar + JRE; the jar is deliberately NOT vendored or auto-fetched (the validated build is a TLA+ Tools nightly, sha256-pinned to the 2026-07-15 run — a hard pin against 'download latest' would fail for everyone), so no stock runner can run it. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-verus	-	the all-length Verus flash-journal crash-safety pilot needs a rustc-pinned prebuilt Verus at VERUS_DIR (see contracts/verification/scripts/fv-external-tools.env); not vendored, so no stock runner can run it. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-crux-ns-ptr	-	the crux-mir implementation-diversity check (ns_ptr_validate vs an independent u64 oracle) needs the schema-8 mir-json rlibs + the SAW-bundle crux-mir-comp locally (see contracts/verification/scripts/fv-external-tools.env); not vendored. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-lean-proto-domain	-	P7 domain-tag drift lint (Lean factoryAddSlotDomain == proto::FACTORY_ADD_SLOT_DOMAIN). Pure Python, no lake build — CI-wirable; enrolled local_documented 2026-08-20 (#664) pending an explicit wiring decision rather than a silent absence from every workflow.
verify-linker-map	-	P1.9 TrustZone memory-map drift gate (.x == proto == sau.rs == Lean). Pure source parse with a wired-in --self-test, no build — CI-wirable; enrolled local_documented 2026-08-20 (#664) pending an explicit wiring decision.
verify-halmos	-	same constraint as verify-bytecode (which invokes the same halmos/run_halmos.sh): the patched halmos toolchain + long symbolic runs stay local/manual (HALMOS-FAST-CI-GATE-FALSE, corrected 2026-07-02). Per-PR bytecode-drift protection is the codehash-freeze + deploy-profile pins in ci.yml (#672). Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-kontrol	-	Kontrol/KEVM symbolic proofs on the deployed bytecode need a K backend (`kup install kontrol` via nix, or the RV docker image); ~5 min build+prove when present, uninstallable on a stock runner. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-parse-transcription	-	the A3.1 in-kernel Yul-parse leg (parseYul c10Source = some c10ProgramFull + elision bridge). Its kernel modules are compiled by lean-fv.yml's `lake build SphincsCVerify` via the root import, and its byte-pin leg runs per-PR in verify-transcription; this focused target (+ its closure echo) stays a local convenience (Makefile note, 2026-07-04). Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-interp	-	the A3.1 interpreter<->bytecode KAT+bulk replay needs the full Lean build + `lake exe verify-interp` over the corpus — heavy; the lighter transcription legs run per-PR (a31-transcription.yml + ci.yml). Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-cavp	-	NIST CAVP SHA-256 conformance: regenerates the embedded vector module (python, idempotent) then `lake exe verify-cavp` over all ShortMsg/LongMsg + Monte Carlo vectors — needs the Lean toolchain + build; runs in no workflow today. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-primitive-kat	-	the per-primitive tweakable-hash KAT (Rust<->Python<->Yul three-way) needs cargo (sim-internals) + python3 + forge on PATH — heavier than the per-PR budget. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-bulk	-	the bulk executable-spec differential needs the Lean build + `lake exe verify-bulk` over the committed BulkVectors.lean artifact (the GEN=1 corpus regen is a separate local flow). Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-exec-gate	-	the Claim-4 trace-gate closure gate lake-builds the TxFlow + Spec.Theorems dep closure and enforces kernel-only axioms on the dump — needs the Lean toolchain; runs in no workflow today. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-forsc-margin	-	the FORS+C grinding-margin guardrail (never weaker than plain FORS at C10 params; fails if the removed forced-zero tree is ever shrunk). Pure-Python arithmetic over params.rs with a wired-in --self-test, no build — CI-wirable; enrolled local_documented 2026-08-20 (#664) pending an explicit wiring decision.
verify-independent-signer	-	leg (2) — the Rust cross-verifier accepting FRESH independent-signer output — already runs per-PR in the ci.yml host-tests job (`cargo test -p sphincs-c10 --test independent_signer_xcheck --release`); the full target adds the pure-Python byte-equivalence leg (~5 s) locally. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).
verify-pins	-	tools/verify_pins.sh supply-chain pin audit (Cargo.lock checksums, git rev= pins, foundry.lock matching checked-out libs, dated-nightly rust-toolchain). Every release-path target depends on it, but no workflow invokes it directly; its deploy-profile codehash-pin substance runs per-PR in the ci.yml contracts jobs. Enrolled 2026-08-20 (#664).

